    "updated_at": "2026-04-04T13:35:34Z",
    "body": "Back in Matrix, @zcorpan pointed out that, in the status quo, \"is an audio or video element\" is unnecessary. I wasn't sure why then, but now I realize that it's because the set-up of `eligible for autoplay` assumes that its 'argument' **is** a media element (i.e., an `audio` or `video` element, in the HTML spec).\n\nSo, @annevk, I think we can delete \"If it is a media element and\" from your suggestion.",
